<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Joseph Bonaparte</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates"><a href="/years/1768">1768</a>–<a href="/years/1844">1844</a></span> · <a href="/centuries/19th-century">19th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Joseph Bonaparte was the elder brother of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a>, who made him king of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/naples">Naples</a> in 1806. In Naples he abolished feudalism, closed monasteries and introduced French administration. In 1808 Napoleon moved him to the throne of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/spain">Spain</a>, where he faced the Peninsular War until his defeat at Vitoria in 1813, and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/joachim-murat">Joachim Murat</a> replaced him in Naples.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/joseph-bonaparte.jpg" alt="Joseph Bonaparte" width="320" height="492" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: François Gérard · Public domain · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Joseph-Bonaparte.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
